  "source_transcript": "Yeah, good. No, good question. So, really and truly, I would say, but and I say this maybe because I've got some biasness in me. But um, do you like do you like pizza? Firstly, exactly. So I would say there's a place called Crisp W Six. Now that is Crisp W Six. So it was actually used to be opened in Hammersmith in in a pub called the Chancellor's Pub. Now it actually got so the Chancellor's Pub, correct, just off Hammersmith by the Apollo, and it was yeah. So was it opened in a pub and it actually was born from just during COVID. Whilst this man called Carl McCluskey just started making pizzas in the back of his garden, and then whilst travelling New York, he sampled the New York scene as far as the pizza. Which a lot of it was was thin crust. He really gravitated towards that and put his own spin as far as making the the dough really really unique. Now that pizza place, whilst being in this very sleepy area of London, became renowned as the best pizza",
